# Wireshark First Capture Notes

## Overview
- Tools used: Wireshark on Kali Linux / Windows
- Captured traffic for: 2 minutes
- Main protocols observed: DNS, HTTP, TCP

## Key Filters & Commands Used
- `dns` — Displays domain name resolution requests (port 53)
- `http.request` — Filters cleartext HTTP GET/POST requests
- `ip.addr == <your-ip>` — Isolates traffic related to host IP

## Findings
- Identified DNS query for `google.com`
- Inspected cleartext HTTP stream for `neverssl.com` using Follow -> TCP Stream
